867
01:22:21.980 --> 01:22:32.529
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): They all lived together in happiness. They learned to sing, and to speak, and to dance together, and to tell the story of their tree, until one day, a great wind came.

868
01:22:32.750 --> 01:22:37.310
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And Little Seed and all of his brothers and sisters blew out into the world.

869
01:22:38.480 --> 01:22:45.839
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Seasons turned, but he stayed a seed, and blew from one place to the next, because he was not sure where he should be planted.

870
01:22:46.600 --> 01:22:49.739
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Sometimes, he yearned to go back home.

871
01:22:50.220 --> 01:22:55.710
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): But he came to believe that the path home was closed to him, and so he never tried to take it.

872
01:22:56.760 --> 01:23:06.880
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And the strangest thing was, when he saw his siblings, and the trees that had grown from seasons past, they could not recognize that he was still a seed.

873
01:23:08.540 --> 01:23:21.949
